problems.problem:
Let $n > 1$ be an integer. Find, with proof, all sequences $x_1$, $x_2$, $\dots$, $x_{n-1}$ of positive integers with the following three properties:

(a) $x_1 < x_2 < \dotsb < x_{n-1}$;
(b) $x_i + x_{n-i} = 2n$ for all $i = 1, 2, \dots , n - 1$;
(c) given any two indices $i$ and $j$ (not necessarily distinct) for which $x_i + x_j < 2n$, there is an index $k$ such that $x_i + x_j = x_k$.
